  "visual_review": "Side-by-side crops at 1:1 (1280x704) on frames 60, 700, 1500, 2050 against the Lanczos-upscaled source. Latent 3D: faithful, visibly sharper, natural skin/teeth/hair detail, nothing invented. SeedVR2: most faithful and sharpest edges, slightly painted skin, practically no new detail. Ultimate (learned 3D latent upscale, denoise 0.25): clean, most new detail (clouds, lashes, facades, signs) but re-interprets freely (sign texts change, moon placed on a tower, slight re-framing). First run with Rodent's bicubic latent upscale: blocky clouds and invented objects (glasses, cap, logo sign, glitch lines) - replaced. Within-shot block borders: worst Latent 3D border (frame 1392, wide shot) shows small details of the singer switching (stockings/tattoos, hair strands); SeedVR2 shows no border jumps.",
